; External variables: at program or unit level, not initialized or
; absolute, a string constant library and symbol, `cvar` with `external`,
; and `name` for one variable only.
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/external/vars.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: vars.pas:6:3: error: 'cvar' without 'external' (a variable for C code to use) is not supported yet
; CHECK: vars.pas:7:3: error: external variable 'd' cannot be initialized
; CHECK: vars.pas:8:24: error: the library name of an external variable must be a string constant
; CHECK: vars.pas:11:3: error: external variable 'local' must be declared at program or unit level
; CHECK-NOT: error:
; RUN: not %pcc --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/external/parse.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck --check-prefix=PARSE %s
; PARSE: parse.pas:3:18: error: 'name' can only be given for one variable
